 ## Stage B2 — BUG-003, round 2's fixes
-- workflow-check.py's `escape_field` keeps a literal backslash, so a name that contains the four characters backslash, x, e, 9 prints exactly like a name holding é (escaped as backslash-x-e-9), and the text backslash, x, 0, a like an escaped line feed; no line or RESULT can be forged (the field never holds a raw line break). Escaping the backslash itself would depart from the agreed escape forms (those of Python's backslashreplace) and change what inventory-check and conformance-check print; no current exact-output entry holds a literal backslash. A lead for a later change to the check's output (security auditor, BUG-003, advisory; the cost restated at round 3).
